%I A398234 #31 Nov 11 2026 10:12:07
%S A398234 5279549641,5279549657,5279552947,5279553341,5279553361,5279623541,
%T A398234 5279623589,5279623621,5279623667,5279623697,5279623759,5279623763,
%U A398234 5279623823,5279623831,5279623891,5279623903,5279623907,5279623931,5279624117,5279624149,5279624177,5279624549
%N A398234 Primes p for which pi_{24;5,23}(p) - pi_{24;1,19}(p) = -1, where pi_{m;a,b,...}(x) is the number of primes <= x which are congruent to a or b or ... (mod m).
%C A398234 From _Leandro Hector Gallego_ and _Jianing Song_: (Start)
%C A398234 This sequence is about one of the 21 prime races modulo 24 between cosets of index 4 in (Z/24Z)*; see A401958 for more details. Specifically, here we have H = {1,19} and S = {5,23}, corresponding to T = {chi_{-3}, chi_{-8}}, where chi_d = (d/.) is the Kronecker symbol viewed as a character modulo N = 24.
%C A398234 This sequence gives primes p such that Sum_{primes q<=p} (chi_{-3}(q) + chi_{-8}(q))/2 = 1.
%C A398234 Assuming GRH and LI (see A401958), the set of x with pi_{24;5,23}(x) > pi_{24;1,19}(x) has logarithmic density 0.99944, making the race between {1,19} and {5,23} the 4th most biased among the 21 races of cosets of index 4 in (Z/24Z)*; see the Zenodo preprint below.
%C A398234 Let D(x) = pi_{24;5,23}(x) - pi_{24;1,19}(x). Below x0 = 7*10^12 there are respectively 30659637567, 30659688364, 30659698140, 30659716342, 30659718072, 30659718286, 30659752652, and 30659759379 primes congruent to 1, 5, 7, 11, 13, 17, 19, or 23 modulo 24, giving D(x0) = 57524. There are 2 sign-changing zones giving a total of 293714 terms below x0:
%C A398234   (1) a(1..1132) = 5279549641-5289063149 (there are 123843 primes a(1) <= p <= a(1132) such that D(p) < 0, with D(p) reaching a minimum of -141 at p = 5286758833);
%C A398234   (2) a(1133..293714) = 6064742035273-6211126435697 (there are 1290674108 primes a(1133) <= p <= a(293714) such that D(p) < 0, with D(p) reaching a minimum of -12136 at p = 6202090143451).
%C A398234 The total number of primes p <= x0 with D(p) < 0 is 1290797951. (End)
%H A398234 Leandro Hector Gallego, <a href="/A398234/b398234.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a> (a(1)-a(1132) from Jianing Song)
%H A398234 Leandro Hector Gallego, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24020025">Logarithmic densities of prime number races between the cosets of a subgroup of index 4 modulo 24</a>, preprint, Zenodo, 2026.
%H A398234 Leandro Hector Gallego, <a href="/A398234/a398234.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..293714</a> (all terms below 7*10^12).
%H A398234 Greg Martin and Daniel Fiorilli, <a href="https://personal.math.ubc.ca/~gerg/slides/Chennai-31Aug10.pdf">Prime number races: An asymptotic formula for the densities</a>, Analytic and Combinatorial Number Theory, Institute of Mathematical Sciences, Chennai, India. August 31, 2010.
%H A398234 Greg Martin, <a href="https://personal.math.ubc.ca/~gerg/slides/Canberra-29Nov18.pdf">Prime number races</a>, Pure Math Seminar, UNSW Canberra. November 29, 2018.
%H A398234 Andrey S. Shchebetov, <a href="https://math101.guru/wp-content/uploads/2018/09/01-A3-Presentation-v7.3EN-no.pdf">Testing Chebyshev's bias for prime numbers up to 10^15</a>, EUCYS 2018.
%H A398234 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chebyshev%27s_bias">Chebyshev's bias</a>.
%o A398234 (PARI) my(k=0); forprime(p=2, 1e11, if(p%24==1||p%24==19, k--); if(p%24==5||p%24==23, k++); if(k==-1, print1(p, ", ")))
%Y A398234 See A401958 for related sequences.
%K A398234 nonn,changed
%O A398234 1,1
%A A398234 _Jianing Song_, Jul 24 2026
